  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "The Sairuki ride wide grass seas, measuring worth in kinship, speed, and remembered routes.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Sairuki follow the pasture line across vast grasslands, moving with horse herds, wagons, and shrine-poles wrapped in wind-torn ribbons. Their loyalties run first to clan and campfire, not to walls, and they respect those who endure hard weather without complaint. Debate is loud, hospitality sacred, and leadership temporary unless renewed by skill, generosity, and success on the open road."
